# rule.forbid.any-time

never declare, store, or pass a time/date/duration as Date, epoch number, bare string, moment/dayjs, or `{ hrs, mins }` bag. use the `iso-time` glossary
- instant → `IsoTimeStamp` (utc, `Z`) · date → `IsoDateStamp` · month → `IsoMonthStamp`
- detached pattern ("when it repeats") → `IsoTimeFloat` (a clock time, no date), `IsoWeekdayFloat`
- duration → `IsoDuration` ('PT30M' | { minutes: 30 }) · ranges → `IsoTimeStampRange` { since, until }
reach for: `asIsoTimeStamp(x)` (cast at the boundary, at once) · `now()` / `today()` (not new Date()) · `addDuration` / `subDuration` · `getDuration({ of: { range } })` · `sumDurations` · `toMilliseconds` (only to hand a raw-ms api)
allowed: a Date/number as transient input to an as* cast at a boundary
docs: `rhx git.repo.get lines --in ehmpathy/iso-time --paths 'readme.md'` · full rule: rule.require.iso-time
enforcement: time field as Date/number/bare string in a domain object, contract, or stored value = blocker; hand-rolled ms arithmetic = blocker
